---
import { chernTrimMasses, sampleChernModel } from '../../../data/part06/ch27TeachingModels.mjs';
const xiInitial = 1;
const V = -0.75;
const v = Math.SQRT1_2 / 2;
const massesInitial = chernTrimMasses(xiInitial, V);
const topologyInitial = sampleChernModel(xiInitial, V, v, 31);
const barHeight = (value) => 52 * Math.min(Math.abs(value), 2.8) / 2.8;
---

<figure class="chapter-visual chern-mass" data-chern-mass>
  <figcaption>
    <strong>原创交互模型：TRIM mass、闭隙点与 Chern 相</strong>
    <span lang="en">Original interactive model: TRIM masses, gap closings, and Chern phases</span>
  </figcaption>

  <div class="chapter-visual__controls">
    <label>
      <span>轨道能级参数 ξ | orbital-level parameter</span>
      <input type="range" min="-2.25" max="2.25" step="0.05" value={xiInitial} data-cm-xi />
      <output data-cm-xi-out>{xiInitial.toFixed(2)}</output>
    </label>
  </div>

  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 360" role="img" aria-labelledby="cm-title cm-desc">
    <title id="cm-title">Chern-model masses at four time-reversal-invariant momenta</title>
    <desc id="cm-desc">The left panel shows the square Brillouin zone and signed masses at Gamma, X, Y, and M. The right panel shows the phase sequence as xi crosses three gap-closing values.</desc>

    <g aria-label="square Brillouin zone and TRIM masses">
      <rect x="65" y="55" width="250" height="250" class="cm-bz" />
      <line x1="190" y1="55" x2="190" y2="305" class="cm-guide" />
      <line x1="65" y1="180" x2="315" y2="180" class="cm-guide" />
      <g data-cm-trim="gamma">
        <circle cx="190" cy="180" r="7" class="cm-trim" />
        <rect x="180" y={180 - barHeight(massesInitial.gamma)} width="20" height={barHeight(massesInitial.gamma)} class:list={['cm-mass', massesInitial.gamma < 0 && 'cm-mass--negative']} data-cm-bar="gamma" />
        <text x="204" y="174">Γ</text>
      </g>
      <g data-cm-trim="x">
        <circle cx="315" cy="180" r="7" class="cm-trim" />
        <rect x="305" y={180 - barHeight(massesInitial.x)} width="20" height={barHeight(massesInitial.x)} class:list={['cm-mass', massesInitial.x < 0 && 'cm-mass--negative']} data-cm-bar="x" />
        <text x="328" y="174">X</text>
      </g>
      <g data-cm-trim="y">
        <circle cx="190" cy="55" r="7" class="cm-trim" />
        <rect x="180" y={55 - barHeight(massesInitial.y)} width="20" height={barHeight(massesInitial.y)} class:list={['cm-mass', massesInitial.y < 0 && 'cm-mass--negative']} data-cm-bar="y" />
        <text x="204" y="49">Y</text>
      </g>
      <g data-cm-trim="m">
        <circle cx="315" cy="55" r="7" class="cm-trim" />
        <rect x="305" y={55 - barHeight(massesInitial.m)} width="20" height={barHeight(massesInitial.m)} class:list={['cm-mass', massesInitial.m < 0 && 'cm-mass--negative']} data-cm-bar="m" />
        <text x="328" y="49">M</text>
      </g>
      <text x="82" y="332">mass bars: above = positive, below/marked = negative</text>
    </g>

    <g aria-label="Chern phase line">
      <line x1="410" y1="180" x2="715" y2="180" class="cm-phase-axis" />
      {[-1.5, 0, 1.5].map((critical) => (
        <g><line x1={562 + critical * 68} y1="112" x2={562 + critical * 68} y2="248" class="cm-critical" /><text x={548 + critical * 68} y="270">{critical.toFixed(1)}</text></g>
      ))}
      <text x="405" y="276">ξ</text>
      <text x="422" y="145">C−=0</text>
      <text x="478" y="145">C−=+1</text>
      <text x="575" y="145">C−=−1</text>
      <text x="674" y="145">C−=0</text>
      <circle cx={562 + xiInitial * 68} cy="180" r="9" class="cm-cursor" data-cm-cursor />
      <text x="430" y="65">V = −0.75, v = √2/4</text>
      <text x="430" y="92">critical ξ: −1.5, 0, +1.5</text>
    </g>
  </svg>

  <div class="chapter-visual__readout" aria-live="polite">
    <span data-cm-masses>mΓ={massesInitial.gamma.toFixed(2)}, mX=mY={massesInitial.x.toFixed(2)}, mM={massesInitial.m.toFixed(2)}</span>
    <span data-cm-gap>sampled minimum gap = {topologyInitial.minimumGap.toFixed(3)}</span>
    <span data-cm-chern>lower-band C− = {topologyInitial.lowerBandChern}; |C−| = {topologyInitial.absoluteChern}</span>
    <strong data-cm-status>One inverted TRIM relative to the others; one chiral branch per edge in the declared model.</strong>
  </div>

  <noscript><p><strong>无 JavaScript 回退 | No-JavaScript fallback:</strong> ξ=1、V=−0.75 时，Γ mass 为负，X/Y/M mass 为正；声明的 $(k_x,k_y)$ 与 Pauli convention 给出低能带 C−=−1，因此 |C−|=1。</p></noscript>

  <div class="chapter-visual__contract">
    <p><strong>模型：</strong><code>h=(v sin ky, v sin kx, ξ+V(cos kx+cos ky))</code>，对应 Martin Eq. 27.1–27.2 的两带 Chern precursor。四个 TRIM mass 分别为 <code>ξ+2V</code>、<code>ξ</code>、<code>ξ</code>、<code>ξ−2V</code>。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Model:</strong> <code>h=(v sin ky, v sin kx, ξ+V(cos kx+cos ky))</code>, the two-band Chern precursor of Martin Eqs. 27.1–27.2. The four TRIM masses are <code>ξ+2V</code>, <code>ξ</code>, <code>ξ</code>, and <code>ξ−2V</code>.</p>
    <p><strong>计算：</strong>页面把归一化 h 向量在每个 BZ 网格 plaquette 上分成两个球面三角形，累计有向固角得到 mapping degree，并按本站 occupied-band convention 取 <code>C−=−degree</code>。在 ξ=−1.5、0、+1.5 处至少一个 TRIM mass 为零，不变量标记为 undefined。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Computation:</strong> each Brillouin-zone plaquette is split into two spherical triangles of the normalized h vector. Their oriented solid angles give the mapping degree, and the declared occupied-band convention sets <code>C−=−degree</code>. At ξ=−1.5, 0, or +1.5 at least one TRIM mass vanishes, so the invariant is reported as undefined.</p>
    <p><strong>边界：</strong>Chern 符号随 momentum orientation、Pauli 轴与带标签改变；|C| 和同一 convention 下的相变差更稳健。该 spinless block 明确破坏 time reversal。它是后续 topological-insulator block picture 的前驱，不是 time-reversal-symmetric 材料的完整模型。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Boundary:</strong> the Chern sign changes with momentum orientation, Pauli axes, and band labels; |C| and phase differences within one convention are more robust. This spinless block explicitly breaks time reversal. It is a precursor to the later block picture, not a complete time-reversal-symmetric material model.</p>
  </div>
</figure>

<script>
  import { chernTrimMasses, sampleChernModel } from '../../../data/part06/ch27TeachingModels.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-chern-mass]').forEach((root) => {
    const xiInput = root.querySelector('[data-cm-xi]');
    if (!(xiInput instanceof HTMLInputElement)) return;
    const setText = (selector, value) => {
      const element = root.querySelector(selector);
      if (element instanceof HTMLElement || element instanceof SVGTextElement) element.textContent = value;
    };
    const update = () => {
      const xi = Number(xiInput.value);
      const masses = chernTrimMasses(xi, -0.75);
      const topology = sampleChernModel(xi, -0.75, Math.SQRT1_2 / 2, 25);
      const cursor = root.querySelector('[data-cm-cursor]');
      if (cursor instanceof SVGCircleElement) cursor.setAttribute('cx', String(562 + xi * 68));
      Object.entries(masses).forEach(([key, value]) => {
        const bar = root.querySelector(`[data-cm-bar="${key}"]`);
        if (!(bar instanceof SVGRectElement)) return;
        const height = 52 * Math.min(Math.abs(value), 2.8) / 2.8;
        const baseline = key === 'gamma' || key === 'x' ? 180 : 55;
        bar.setAttribute('height', height.toFixed(2));
        bar.setAttribute('y', (value >= 0 ? baseline - height : baseline).toFixed(2));
        bar.classList.toggle('cm-mass--negative', value < 0);
      });
      setText('[data-cm-xi-out]', xi.toFixed(2));
      setText('[data-cm-masses]', `mΓ=${masses.gamma.toFixed(2)}, mX=mY=${masses.x.toFixed(2)}, mM=${masses.m.toFixed(2)}`);
      if (topology.gapClosed) {
        setText('[data-cm-gap]', 'minimum gap = 0 at a TRIM');
        setText('[data-cm-chern]', 'lower-band C− undefined');
        setText('[data-cm-status]', 'Bulk gap closed: adjacent Chern phases meet.');
        return;
      }
      setText('[data-cm-gap]', `sampled minimum gap = ${topology.minimumGap.toFixed(3)}`);
      setText('[data-cm-chern]', `lower-band C− = ${topology.lowerBandChern}; |C−| = ${topology.absoluteChern}`);
      const status = topology.absoluteChern === 1
        ? 'One inverted TRIM sector; one chiral branch per edge in the declared model.'
        : 'No net sphere wrapping; the declared lower band is Chern-trivial.';
      setText('[data-cm-status]', status);
    };
    xiInput.addEventListener('input', update);
    update();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .chern-mass svg { width: 100%; max-height: 27rem; }
  .chern-mass text { fill: currentColor; font-size: 13px; }
  .cm-bz { fill: none; stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3); stroke-width: 2; }
  .cm-guide { stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-5); stroke-dasharray: 5 5; }
  .cm-trim { fill: var(--sl-color-gray-2); }
  .cm-mass { fill: var(--sl-color-text-accent); }
  .cm-mass--negative { fill: var(--sl-color-red-high, #b42318); }
  .cm-phase-axis { stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3); stroke-width: 2; }
  .cm-critical { stroke: var(--sl-color-red-high, #b42318); stroke-width: 2; stroke-dasharray: 6 5; }
  .cm-cursor { fill: var(--sl-color-accent-high); stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-7); stroke-width: 2; }
</style>
